ristic p, integer 0 ≤ λ < p, and admissible lattice M in the characteristic-zero irreducible sl(2,C)-module V(λ), prove M ⊗_Z K is irreducible as an L(K)-module, where L(K) is the Chevalley form (including characteristic 2).\\\",\\\"definitions_used\\\":[\\\"Use the source-context definitions: x,y,h satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=-2y, [x,y]=h; V(λ) is the (λ+1)-dimensional characteristic-zero highest-weight module with highest vector v and xv=0, hv=λv.\\\",\\\"The divided-power integral enveloping algebra U_Z is generated by x^(r)/r! and y^(r)/r!; an admissible lattice M is a full Z-lattice stable under U_Z.\\\",\\\"L(K) acts through the reductions of x,y,h. Irreducibility means nonzero and having no proper nonzero K-linear submodule.\\\"],\\\"proof\\\":\\\"Put e_i=y^i v/i! for 0≤i≤λ. These form a C-basis. From [x,y]=h and [h,y]=-2y, induction gives x e_i=(λ-i+1)e_(i-1), y e_i=(i+1)e_(i+1), with out-of-range terms zero. Iterating these formulas gives, for divided powers X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r!, X_r e_i=binom(λ-i+r,r)e_(i-r) and Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_(i+r), again zero when the index is out of range. In particular all X_r,Y_r preserve the standard Z-lattice M0 with basis (e_0,…,e_λ).\\\\n\\\\nFix p and let R=Z_(p). Regard M_R=R⊗_Z M as a full R-lattice in V(λ), and M0_R similarly. Since M is U_Z-stable, M_R is stable under the image A_R of U_Z⊗R. In the standard basis, X_λ sends e_λ to e_0 and kills e_i for i<λ; Y_λ sends e_0 to e_λ and kills e_i for i>0. Thus P_λ=Y_λX_λ is the matrix unit E_λλ. For every i, X_(λ-i)P_λ=E_iλ: it sends e_λ to e_i and kills the other basis vectors. For every j, P_λY_(λ-j)=binom(λ,j)E_λj. Because λ<p, both λ! and binom(λ,j) are units in R. Consequently E_λj and then E_ij=E_iλE_λj belong to A_R for all i,j. (When λ=0 this says the identity matrix belongs to A_R.)\\\\n\\\\nThe lattice M_R is therefore stable under every standard matrix unit E_ij. Write vectors in the basis e_i. The coordinate ideals I_i={a∈Q : a e_i∈M_R} are fractional R-ideals: they are nonzero fractional ideals because M_R is a full lattice. Stability under E_ij implies I_j⊆I_i, and reversing i,j gives equality. Moreover, for any vector of M_R, its individual coordinates times their basis vectors belong to M_R by applying E_ii. It follows that M_R=⊕_i I_i e_i=I M0_R for one fractional ideal I of R. Since R is a discrete valuation ring, I=p^nR for some integer n. Hence M_R/pM_R, with its induced action, is isomorphic to M0_R/pM0_R. Localization and reduction identify this quotient with M⊗_Z F_p. Extending scalars from F_p to K identifies M⊗_Z K with the scalar extension of the standard reduced module.\\\\n\\\\nIt remains to prove that this standard module is irreducible, rather than infer it from distinct h-weights. In characteristic p, for r≤λ<p, r! is invertible, so X_r and Y_r are scalar multiples of compositions of the Lie operators x and y. The matrix-unit construction above uses only r≤λ and coefficients binom(λ,j) that are nonzero modulo p. It therefore constructs every E_ij as a K-linear combination of compositions of x and y on the reduced standard module, also when p=2. Any L(K)-submodule is stable under x,y and their compositions, hence under all E_ij. If it contains a nonzero vector with a nonzero i-th coordinate, applying E_ji gives a nonzero multiple of e_j for each j; applying matrix units then yields every basis vector. Thus it is the whole module. The module has dimension λ+1 and is nonzero. For λ=0 it is one-dimensional and the same conclusion holds directly. This proves the target for every stated M, p, and K.\\\",\\\"cited_results\\\":[],\\\"unresolved_points\\\":[],\\\"boundary_cases\\\":\\\"λ=0 gives a one-dimensional trivial module. Characteristic 2 is included: the proof uses no distinction of h-weights, and all required factorials and binomial coefficients are units modulo p because λ<p. The arbitrary admissible lattice is handled by localization and the matrix-unit argument; it is not assumed to be the standard lattice.\\\"}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"01a16793-ada8-7ae3-b31b-f42547f19fca","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2015,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3429,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2221},"total_tokens":5444,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_04b1fd63aed1d9ac016adb0718498c8191b7d385bce9738bc4":{"input_tokens":30,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_04b1fd63aed1d9ac016adb071a940881919b7ccb9589db74de":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_04b1fd63aed1d9ac016adb071d1c7c819191255b175451f852":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_04b1fd63aed1d9ac016adb071f9f78819182557e650e7cff4c":{"input_tokens":30,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_04b1fd63aed1d9ac016adb072201a48191891207756c7adf14":{"input_tokens":30,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_04b1fd63aed1d9ac016adb0737ad648191bbde1b442cbfa8dd":{"input_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1208},"fco_01a16793-b746-7913-87a8-f9494d08d133":{"input_tokens":106,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"content":[{"input_tokens":106,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}]},"fco_01a16793-c135-7e82-ac9c-9b5bcbac1482":{"input_tokens":39,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"content":[{"input_tokens":39,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}]},"fco_01a16793-ca06-7e60-b527-6ce2d2296333":{"input_tokens":979,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"content":[{"input_tokens":979,"cached_tokens":0,"cache